hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1536","I am Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadafi, from Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukayr. Al-Layth narrated to me, on the authority of Khalid, who is Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Saeed, who is Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, that he said: I and Abu Salamah bin Abd entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah. The Most Gracious, and we found him standing with a garment praying over him, so he mentioned some of the hadith and said: “We came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he left. For some of his needs, I poured ablution for him, and he ablution and wrapped himself in his garment, so I stood to his left, and he placed me to his right, and another came, and he stood On his left, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward to pray, and we prayed with him, so he prayed thirteen rak’ahs reciting the Witr prayer.”"
